就像，没错。

1034
00:46:20.520 --> 00:46:20.780
I don't know.
我不知道。

1035
00:46:21.040 --> 00:46:23.080
Again, that could be total malarkey.
再说一次，这可能完全是胡说八道。

1036
00:46:23.260 --> 00:46:24.400
But I mean, it tracks.
但我觉得，这说得通。

1037
00:46:24.680 --> 00:46:25.640
I've been really into.
我最近特别迷。

1038
00:46:26.180 --> 00:46:29.940
There's a show about animals on Netflix, and we watched the one about dogs.
Netflix上有一个关于动物的节目，我们看了关于狗的那一集。

1039
00:46:30.140 --> 00:46:31.100
It's so good.
太棒了。

1040
00:46:31.700 --> 00:46:31.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1041
00:46:32.160 --> 00:46:36.800
And dogs do this little sniffy, snorty thing when they're, you know how they play fight?
狗在玩耍打闹的时候会发出那种嗅鼻子的哼哼声，你知道吗？

1042
00:46:37.000 --> 00:46:37.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

1043
00:46:37.160 --> 00:46:39.520
And it's to let the other dog know that I'm not serious.
那是为了让对方知道我不是认真的。

1044
00:46:39.720 --> 00:46:44.660
And so if you hear your dog, and now my little two Chihuahua rescues, when they play, I hear it.
所以如果你听到你的狗发出这种声音，现在我那两只吉娃娃救援犬玩耍时，我就能听到。

1045
00:46:44.740 --> 00:46:44.880
They go.
它们会发出那种声音。

1046
00:46:47.000 --> 00:46:47.400
Really?
真的吗？

1047
00:46:47.400 --> 00:46:50.100
And it's like, I'm just having fun.
就像是在说，我只是在玩而已。

1048
00:46:50.480 --> 00:46:57.000
That must be so hard on dogs who, like, want to be aggressive, but have allergies, where they're, like, trying to, like, really, like, big dog another dog.
那对于那些想表现得凶猛，却有鼻过敏的狗来说一定很难，它们想表现得像只大狗去压制另一只狗，结果却……

1049
00:46:57.180 --> 00:46:58.600
And they're just like, yeah, like a pug.
它们就像，没错，就像哈巴狗那样。

1050
00:46:58.780 --> 00:47:01.520
Like, a pug can never be taken seriously when he's trying to, like.
比如，一只哈巴狗想表现得凶一点时，根本没人会当真。

1051
00:47:01.920 --> 00:47:02.820
Be aggressive.
要强势一点。

1052
00:47:03.020 --> 00:47:03.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1053
00:47:03.240 --> 00:47:03.720
He's like, I mean it.
他当时就像是，我是认真的。

1054
00:47:03.720 --> 00:47:04.420
I'm actually angry.
我是真的生气了。

1055
00:47:04.640 --> 00:47:05.900
I really mean it, guys.
伙计们，我是说真的。

1056
00:47:06.220 --> 00:47:07.520
Like, no, you don't.
就像是，不，你才没有。

1057
00:47:07.520 --> 00:47:08.080
No, you don't.
不，你没有。

1058
00:47:08.080 --> 00:47:08.860
You're being silly.
你太傻了。

1059
00:47:09.460 --> 00:47:10.260
That's funny.
真好笑。

1060
00:47:11.280 --> 00:47:13.120
Do you get recognized as Gabe?
你会因为盖博这个角色被认出来吗？

1061
00:47:14.120 --> 00:47:14.920
Sometimes, yeah.
有时候会，是的。

1062
00:47:15.220 --> 00:47:16.000
It happens sometimes.
偶尔会发生。

1063
00:47:16.000 --> 00:47:16.880
And what is that like?
那是什么感觉？

1064
00:47:16.880 --> 00:47:19.520
I had a really bad one recently because I saw it.
我最近经历过一次特别糟糕的，因为我亲眼目睹了那一幕。

1065
00:47:19.860 --> 00:47:22.960
So I'm making this show now, this, like, stop motion show.
当时我正在制作一部定格动画剧集。

1066
00:47:23.100 --> 00:47:27.900
And in it, there's, like, a lactation station, you know, that they have at the airport.
剧里有个哺乳室，你知道的，就是机场里那种。

1067
00:47:28.140 --> 00:47:30.120
And we were getting designs for them.
我们当时正在设计那个场景。

1068
00:47:30.240 --> 00:47:32.400
And I was like, oh, I want something really simple.
我就说，噢，我想要那种非常简洁的风格。

1069
00:47:32.660 --> 00:47:33.940
And I was in an airport.
当时我正好在机场。

1070
00:47:34.160 --> 00:47:36.220
There was an empty lactation station.
那里有个空着的哺乳室。

1071
00:47:36.240 --> 00:47:41.640
And I wanted to send a picture to the production designer to be like, this is what we're going for.
我想拍张照发给美术指导，告诉他这就是我们想要的效果。

1072
00:47:41.720 --> 00:47:43.040
This is a perfect example, right?
这是一个完美的例子，对吧？

1073
00:47:43.640 --> 00:47:46.840
So I started to take a picture of the lactation station.
于是我就开始拍那个哺乳室。

1074
00:47:47.100 --> 00:47:50.720
As someone came up to me and was like, hey, man, you were Gabe on The Office.
这时有个人走过来对我说，嘿，伙计，你是在《办公室》里演盖博的那个人吧。

1075
00:47:50.960 --> 00:47:54.220
And it's not lost on me that Gabe is, in many ways, quite a creepy character.
我当然知道盖博在很多方面都是个相当令人毛骨悚然的角色。

1076
00:47:54.220 --> 00:48:02.440
And so this guy just saw me by myself in an airport photographing a lactation station like a true predator from hell.
所以那个人看到我独自一人在机场对着哺乳室拍照，简直就像个来自地狱的变态。

1077
00:48:02.640 --> 00:48:04.680
I mean, like, that's an insane thing to do, right?
我是说，这行为简直太疯狂了，对吧？

1078
00:48:04.760 --> 00:48:05.280
To take a picture.
去拍照什么的。

1079
00:48:05.420 --> 00:48:06.860
Like, he has no context.
他完全不了解前因后果。

1080
00:48:07.020 --> 00:48:09.580
And if I say, this is for a show.
如果我说，这是为了拍戏。

1081
00:48:09.740 --> 00:48:10.720
That sounds even worse.
那听起来反而更糟。

1082
00:48:10.880 --> 00:48:11.900
It's like, it's for a show?
就像是，为了拍戏？

1083
00:48:12.080 --> 00:48:12.560
Really, buddy?
真的吗，伙计？

1084
00:48:12.560 --> 00:48:23.020
Like, and so it was, that was a truly mortifying where I'm like, I, he must think I'm like, that Gabe is like a toned down version of me based on, based on that experience.
所以那次经历真的让我感到羞愧难当，我想他肯定觉得盖博那个角色还是我性格的收敛版呢。

1085
00:48:23.420 --> 00:48:26.540
But yeah, people, people sometimes will recognize me from the show.
不过是的，人们有时确实会因为那部剧认出我来。

1086
00:48:26.820 --> 00:48:29.120
So after The Office, you did Silicon Valley.
《办公室》之后，你又演了《硅谷》。

1087
00:48:29.120 --> 00:48:30.620
You've done all these other things.
你还演过其他这么多作品。

1088
00:48:31.020 --> 00:48:35.920
Do you still get approached more for being on The Office or for other roles?
大家找你合影是因为《办公室》多一些，还是因为其他角色？

1089
00:48:36.020 --> 00:48:37.180
Or is it pretty 50-50?
还是说差不多五五开？

1090
00:48:37.760 --> 00:48:42.160
I'd say it's like probably 50-50 with The Office and then everything else I've ever done.
我觉得大概是五五开吧，一半是因为《办公室》，另一半是因为我做过的所有其他事情。

1091
00:48:42.480 --> 00:48:46.000
Like, so it's like the single thing, maybe, well, I don't know.
所以这可能是单一作品里占比最高的，嗯，我也不确定。

1092
00:48:46.180 --> 00:48:48.700
Silicon Valley, yeah, it's probably like around 50-50.
《硅谷》的话，大概也是五五开吧。

1093
00:48:48.800 --> 00:48:49.160
It depends.
这得看情况。

1094
00:48:49.300 --> 00:48:50.560
It's like demographically specific.
这取决于人口统计学特征。

1095
00:48:50.860 --> 00:48:51.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1096
00:48:51.440 --> 00:48:51.780
You know?
你懂的吧？

1097
00:48:51.960 --> 00:48:55.140
And it's interesting, like if it's younger people, it's probably The Office.
很有趣的是，如果是年轻人，大概率是因为《办公室》。

1098
00:48:55.520 --> 00:48:57.220
If it's like really young people.
如果是非常年轻的人的话。

1099
00:48:57.440 --> 00:49:03.780
I think it's so sweet to me that kids find it so comforting that it's a kind of emotional wallpaper.
我觉得孩子们能从中获得慰藉，把它当成一种情感背景墙，这让我觉得非常暖心。

1100
00:49:03.780 --> 00:49:12.440
Like people who've watched it a million times will turn it on as a way of feeling like they're kind of among their friends or in a kind of soothing, warm, silly environment.
那些看过无数遍的人会把它当作一种陪伴，感觉就像置身于朋友之中，或者处于一种舒缓、温暖、有趣的氛围里。

1101
00:49:12.460 --> 00:49:13.900
I think it's so sweet.
我觉得这太贴心了。

1102
00:49:13.900 --> 00:49:24.420
And so it's like nice when it's like some, you know, whatever, 19-year-old who's immersed in the Scranton paper industry fictional world.
所以看到像什么，你知道，随便什么19岁的年轻人，沉浸在斯克兰顿造纸业的虚构世界里，感觉真好。

1103
00:49:24.500 --> 00:49:25.500
I think that's so sweet.
我觉得这太贴心了。

1104
00:49:25.720 --> 00:49:26.460
I like that.
我喜欢这样。

1105
00:49:26.700 --> 00:49:28.260
Have you re-watched the show?
你有重温过这部剧吗？

1106
00:49:28.420 --> 00:49:28.960
Some of it.
看过一部分。

1107
00:49:28.960 --> 00:49:31.580
But I hate watching anything I'm in, so not that stuff.
但我讨厌看自己演的东西，所以没看那些部分。

1108
00:49:31.700 --> 00:49:34.240
But I'd already watched the show so much when I came up.
不过在我加入之前，我已经看过很多遍这部剧了。

1109
00:49:34.340 --> 00:49:39.460
I think I would re-watch the show a lot before I was on the show, but I haven't done like the wall-to-wall re-watch.
我想在参演之前我重温过很多次，但我还没试过那种从头到尾的重温。

1110
00:49:39.880 --> 00:49:40.780
We hadn't either.
我们也没试过。

1111
00:49:40.940 --> 00:49:42.400
This is the first time for us.
这是我们第一次这样看。

1112
00:49:42.720 --> 00:49:44.080
I'd seen episodes here and there.
我以前零零散散看过一些剧集。

1113
00:49:44.200 --> 00:49:44.780
We've talked about that.
我们聊过这个。

1114
00:49:44.780 --> 00:49:44.920
Yeah.
是啊。

1115
00:49:44.960 --> 00:49:49.700
But this is really our first time to see some of these episodes in a long time since they aired.
但这是我们自播出以来，时隔许久第一次看其中一些剧集。

1116
00:49:49.700 --> 00:49:56.480
Does it feel like, does watching the show feel like you're looking at a photo album of your friends and your life in a way?
看这部剧的时候，会不会感觉像是在翻看朋友和自己生活的相册？

1117
00:49:56.560 --> 00:50:02.020
Or does it feel like you can sort of suspend disbelief and get lost in the like story of the show?
还是说你能够暂时放下现实，沉浸在剧中的故事里？

1118
00:50:02.140 --> 00:50:05.840
Like are you able to invest in the fictional reality of the show when you're watching it?
也就是说，你在看的时候能投入到剧中的虚构现实里吗？

1119
00:50:06.020 --> 00:50:06.840
I think so.
我想可以。

1120
00:50:07.060 --> 00:50:10.300
Because of the passage of time, it's both things.
因为时间的流逝，这两种感觉都有。

1121
00:50:10.460 --> 00:50:13.060
So I have a lot of nostalgic thoughts and feelings.
所以我有很多怀旧的思绪和感受。

1122
00:50:13.060 --> 00:50:15.160
I get really sentimental when I'm watching it.
看的时候我真的会变得很感伤。

1123
00:50:15.260 --> 00:50:18.620
I remember parts of my life that were happening when we were making those episodes.
我会想起拍摄那些剧集时我生活中发生的事情。

1124
00:50:19.700 --> 00:50:21.700
Miss people when I watch it.
看的时候会想念大家。

1125
00:50:21.920 --> 00:50:30.760
But I can also, when I watch it, what's weird is I have images of all the things you can't see in the episode.
但与此同时，奇怪的是，当我观看时，脑海里会出现所有你在剧集中看不到的画面。

1126
00:50:30.760 --> 00:50:40.080
So like I can feel Brian Whittle holding his boom above my desk in a scene when I'm watching the re-watch.
比如在重温时，我能感觉到布莱恩·惠特尔在场景里把吊杆麦克风举在我的办公桌上方。

1127
00:50:40.260 --> 00:50:44.580
You know, I can like feel where, oh, that video village was over in the conference room for this one.
你知道，我能感觉到，哦，这一集的监视器村当时是在会议室那边。

1128
00:50:44.820 --> 00:50:46.940
And Kelly's shouting out some safety meeting.
还有凯利在喊着什么安全会议。

1129
00:50:46.940 --> 00:50:51.420
So it's like all of the behind the camera stuff pops into my head as well.
所以镜头背后的那些事儿也会一股脑儿涌进我的脑海。

1130
00:50:51.660 --> 00:50:56.800
But then at the same time, I have found myself getting invested in the characters.
但与此同时，我也发现自己会投入到角色中去。

1131
00:50:56.820 --> 00:51:02.220
Like I personally feel that Aaron is not the one for Andy.
比如我个人觉得艾琳并不适合安迪。

1132
00:51:02.540 --> 00:51:03.260
Not at all.
一点也不。

1133
00:51:03.560 --> 00:51:04.420
And I am getting angry.
我甚至会感到生气。

1134
00:51:04.520 --> 00:51:08.360
It's being shoved down my throat that I'm being told that they're the perfect couple.
剧情硬塞给我，告诉我他们是完美的一对。

1135
00:51:08.360 --> 00:51:11.960
When I actually feel like Andy is thriving with his current girlfriend.
可我实际上觉得安迪和现在的女朋友在一起过得很好。

1136
00:51:12.260 --> 00:51:12.780
Jessica.
杰西卡。

1137
00:51:13.020 --> 00:51:13.340
Jessica.
杰西卡。

1138
00:51:13.720 --> 00:51:13.920
Yeah.
是啊。

1139
00:51:13.920 --> 00:51:14.820
Is great.
她很棒。

1140
00:51:15.120 --> 00:51:15.640
I like Jessica.
我喜欢杰西卡。

1141
00:51:15.980 --> 00:51:16.200
Yeah.
是啊。

1142
00:51:16.480 --> 00:51:16.980
You know?
你懂吗？

1143
00:51:17.360 --> 00:51:18.640
So I don't know.
所以我不知道。

1144
00:51:18.760 --> 00:51:22.900
So I do, I have like some fan reactions when I watch the show as well.
所以我确实也会像粉丝一样对剧集做出反应。

1145
00:51:23.880 --> 00:51:24.940
What about you, Ange?
你呢，安吉？

1146
00:51:25.200 --> 00:51:27.740
Oh, I mean, I think you said that so well.
哦，我是说，你表达得太好了。

1147
00:51:27.880 --> 00:51:29.160
That's exactly how I feel.
我的感觉完全一样。

1148
00:51:29.420 --> 00:51:30.560
It's both for me.
对我来说两者都有。

1149
00:51:30.700 --> 00:51:33.140
It's a photo album and I'm in the audience.
它既是相册，我也像个观众。

1150
00:51:33.140 --> 00:51:34.820
And I kind of switch back and forth.
我会在这两种状态间来回切换。

1151
00:51:35.340 --> 00:51:42.360
I have really strong memories of episodes, you know, when things were happening in my life.
我对剧集真的有很深刻的记忆，你知道，就是在我生活中发生某些事情的时候。

1152
00:51:42.820 --> 00:51:44.900
And I watch it with that layer.
我带着那种心境去看剧。

1153
00:51:45.380 --> 00:51:45.430
Wow.
哇。

1154
00:51:45.560 --> 00:51:45.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1155
00:51:45.680 --> 00:51:50.220
So it's not even just the environment of the set, but it's the environment of your life at that time.
所以这不仅仅是拍摄现场的环境，更是你当时生活环境的投射。

1156
00:51:50.580 --> 00:51:50.630
Yeah.
没错。

1157
00:51:50.700 --> 00:51:50.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1158
00:51:51.140 --> 00:51:51.820
That's fascinating.
这太迷人了。

1159
00:51:51.820 --> 00:51:59.160
So it was, what, nine years of our life and, you know, babies were born and family members passed away.
那可是我们九年的生活，你知道，有孩子出生，也有家人离世。

1160
00:51:59.540 --> 00:52:01.900
And it's a lot of life happens in nine years.
九年里真的发生了太多事。

1161
00:52:02.040 --> 00:52:07.900
And I just watched that play out through this other filter of being a character.
我只是通过扮演角色这一层滤镜，看着这一切上演。

1162
00:52:08.120 --> 00:52:09.540
It's kind of, it's really surreal.
这感觉有点……真的很超现实。

1163
00:52:10.120 --> 00:52:10.900
That's trippy.
太奇妙了。

1164
00:52:11.160 --> 00:52:11.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1165
00:52:11.620 --> 00:52:14.620
A friend of mine said to me, I was like talking about some, maybe New York or something.
我有个朋友曾跟我说，当时我可能在聊纽约什么的。

1166
00:52:14.720 --> 00:52:17.240
And she goes, well, places aren't places as much as their times.
她说，地方本身并不重要，重要的是那个地方所代表的时光。

1167
00:52:17.240 --> 00:52:20.140
Like when you think of a place, often you're thinking of a time.
就像当你想到一个地方时，你往往想到的是一段时光。

1168
00:52:20.560 --> 00:52:20.760
Yeah.
没错。

1169
00:52:20.900 --> 00:52:26.320
And so it's not necessarily the geography of the place, but it's the sort of psychic place you were in in your life, right?
所以这不一定是地理意义上的地方，而是你当时在生活中所处的心理位置，对吧？

1170
00:52:26.380 --> 00:52:29.180
Like where, what was happening or who you were at that time.
比如当时发生了什么，或者你当时是个什么样的人。

1171
00:52:29.720 --> 00:52:32.800
It's so interesting that it's the show where you're being somebody different.
最有趣的是，这是一部让你扮演不同角色的剧。

1172
00:52:33.260 --> 00:52:39.240
Like you're playing a different person, but also you were a different person in your life at that time, right?
你不仅在扮演另一个人，而且你当时在现实生活中也是个不同的人，对吧？

1173
00:52:39.300 --> 00:52:40.700
Like the circumstances of your life were different.
比如你当时的生活境遇不同。

1174
00:52:40.780 --> 00:52:41.860
Your relationships were different.
你的人际关系也不同。

1175
00:52:41.960 --> 00:52:42.480
Everything was different.
一切都不同。

1176
00:52:42.920 --> 00:52:43.860
Can I ask just like one more?
我能再问一个问题吗？

1177
00:52:43.960 --> 00:52:44.620
I'm just curious.
我只是很好奇。

1178
00:52:44.740 --> 00:52:45.140
Yes, yes.
可以，当然可以。

1179
00:52:45.140 --> 00:52:51.520
For you guys, if there's something like you guys could go back and tell yourselves, like in that Our Town style, like what would you,
对你们来说，如果能像《小城风光》那样回到过去告诉自己一些事，你们会……

1180
00:52:51.820 --> 00:53:00.920
like if you could go back to like season one and visit with you, like as your own like fairy godmother, ghost of Christmas future or whatever, like what would you say?
比如如果你能回到第一季去见当时的自己，就像作为自己的神仙教母，或者圣诞未来幽灵什么的，你会说什么？

1181
00:53:01.180 --> 00:53:02.820
Or maybe that's too hard to question.
或者这个问题太难了？

1182
00:53:03.320 --> 00:53:03.700
Hmm.
嗯。

1183
00:53:03.700 --> 00:53:13.060
I would say I think there are a lot of ways that I know how to advocate for myself professionally now that I had to really learn on the go.
我会说，我觉得现在我知道很多在职业生涯中为自己争取权益的方法，而这些都是我当时必须在工作中边做边学的。

1184
00:53:13.240 --> 00:53:19.080
And I feel like in some cases, I even got like some bad advice, you know.
而且我觉得在某些情况下，我甚至得到了一些糟糕的建议，你知道的。

1185
00:53:19.360 --> 00:53:30.020
There were ways where like as you're kind of an up-and-coming actor and maybe you're suddenly on this hit show, there are a lot of people that have ideas for you professionally.
当你作为一个冉冉升起的新星，突然出演了一部热门剧集时，会有很多人对你的职业生涯指手画脚。

1186
00:53:30.020 --> 00:53:34.240
And I was just happy being on the office.
但我当时在《办公室》里就很开心了。

1187
00:53:34.720 --> 00:53:36.420
I didn't need an and.
我不需要什么附加条件。

1188
00:53:36.700 --> 00:53:41.380
I didn't need to also have a product line or also be a movie star.
我不需要去搞什么产品线，也不需要非得成为电影明星。

1189
00:53:41.600 --> 00:53:48.020
And yet I felt the energy coming at me, telling me I needed to do all this more.
然而我却感受到了那种压力，有人告诉我我需要做更多的事情。

1190
00:53:48.900 --> 00:53:52.480
And I think in some ways, you know,
我觉得在某些方面，你知道，

1191
00:53:52.640 --> 00:54:02.200
I would do the TV show and then I would spend my hiatus doing all the more that everyone was telling me that I wanted and that I had to do and that this is what you do next.
我拍完电视剧，假期里还要去忙那些别人告诉我我想要做、必须做、以及下一步该做的事情。

1192
00:54:02.200 --> 00:54:10.620
And the truth is, is I just wanted to spend my hiatus traveling and enjoying my life and being in love.
但事实是，我只想在假期里去旅行，享受生活，谈一场恋爱。

1193
00:54:11.280 --> 00:54:20.060
And sometimes I look back on that time and I think, wow, I was just too busy doing a bunch of things that I felt like were expected of me.
有时回首那段时光，我会想，哇，我当时真是太忙了，忙着做一堆我觉得别人期待我做的事。

1194
00:54:20.220 --> 00:54:23.660
But my truth was, I just want to be on this TV show.
但我的真实想法是，我只想演好这部电视剧。

1195
00:54:23.840 --> 00:54:24.360
I love it.
我热爱它。

1196
00:54:24.440 --> 00:54:24.960
I'm happy.
我很满足。

1197
00:54:25.200 --> 00:54:26.220
This is enough.
这就足够了。

1198
00:54:26.220 --> 00:54:34.280
And it took me a really long time to get to a place where I didn't let other people's idea of what my life should be.
我花了很长时间才达到一种境界，不再让别人对我的生活指手画脚。

1199
00:54:34.360 --> 00:54:40.460
Like I figured out what my ambition is in life, but I spent a lot of years.
我终于弄清楚了自己的人生抱负，但我确实花了很多年。

1200
00:54:40.920 --> 00:54:41.780
I don't know.
我不知道。

1201
00:54:41.900 --> 00:54:47.620
I mean, I don't I don't necessarily regret any of those movies or any of those experiences or any of those things.
我的意思是，我并不一定后悔拍过那些电影，或者经历过那些事，或者做过那些选择。

1202
00:54:47.620 --> 00:54:54.300
But I think it's a life lesson coming to a place where you're like, well, what's enough for me is OK.
但我认为这是一种人生经验，当你达到某种境界，你会觉得，嗯，对我来说够了就好。

1203
00:54:54.780 --> 00:54:55.720
Yes, that's right.
是的，没错。

1204
00:54:56.420 --> 00:54:59.220
Want or need things other people need.
去追求或需要别人所需要的东西。

1205
00:54:59.460 --> 00:55:00.960
What I need is enough.
我所需要的已经足够了。

1206
00:55:01.100 --> 00:55:01.580
And that's OK.
这样也挺好。

1207
00:55:01.780 --> 00:55:01.980
Yeah.
是啊。

1208
00:55:02.240 --> 00:55:09.060
And I think it's even still shocking to people when I say, no, the podcast is enough.
而且我觉得，当我告诉别人“不，做播客就足够了”时，他们依然会感到震惊。

1209
00:55:09.240 --> 00:55:09.960
I enjoy this.
我很享受这个过程。

1210
00:55:10.120 --> 00:55:12.140
I like concentrating on it.
我喜欢专注于此。

1211
00:55:12.260 --> 00:55:13.660
I like this being my one thing.
我喜欢把它当作我唯一的事业。

1212
00:55:13.780 --> 00:55:14.580
I think maybe that's me.
我想也许我就是这样的人。

1213
00:55:14.580 --> 00:55:23.480
Maybe I'm like a monogamous worker, like I have a job I like to do and that's the job I like to do and fully and I enjoy it.
也许我是一个“职场一夫一妻制”者，我有一份喜欢的工作，那就是我全心全意想做的工作，我很享受它。

1214
00:55:23.600 --> 00:55:25.060
And then I like to put it away.
然后我喜欢在工作结束后把它放下。

1215
00:55:25.300 --> 00:55:27.580
Like I don't need a lot of ands.
我不需要太多的“额外附加”。

1216
00:55:27.740 --> 00:55:28.140
I don't.
真的不需要。

1217
00:55:28.460 --> 00:55:29.620
So that's a great.
所以这很棒。

1218
00:55:29.840 --> 00:55:34.080
I wish I could have like told myself to trust that more in me.
我真希望自己早点告诉自己，要多相信这一点。

1219
00:55:34.200 --> 00:55:41.000
It's so noisy, probably when you write like and if all of a sudden you're on the show and it's a success and it's the cacophony of that and all of that.
当你成名时，外界的声音太嘈杂了，尤其是当你突然出演了一部剧并大获成功，那种喧嚣和纷扰会接踵而至。

1220
00:55:41.000 --> 00:55:41.380
It is.
确实如此。

1221
00:55:41.740 --> 00:55:43.760
And all the projection that it cooks up and everything.
还有随之而来的一切投射和揣测。

1222
00:55:43.760 --> 00:55:52.500
I think there's a lot of like fear based sort of communication in that, too, which is like, well, listen, if you don't do this now, it's not going to be there later.
我觉得其中也包含了很多基于恐惧的沟通，就像是，“听着，如果你现在不抓住机会，以后就没机会了”。

1223
00:55:52.620 --> 00:55:55.820
No one's going to want you later if you don't do this now.
“如果你现在不干，以后就没人会要你了。”

1224
00:55:55.960 --> 00:55:56.120
Right.
没错。

1225
00:55:56.260 --> 00:56:01.440
Or you won't work later if you're not working now or any of it, you know.
或者“如果你现在不工作，以后就没工作了”，诸如此类，你懂的。

1226
00:56:01.680 --> 00:56:03.200
And so you're like, oh, my God.
所以你会想，天哪。

1227
00:56:03.320 --> 00:56:03.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1228
00:56:03.580 --> 00:56:04.020
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1229
00:56:04.080 --> 00:56:05.460
I don't I don't want this to go away.
我不想让这一切消失。

1230
00:56:06.060 --> 00:56:11.020
So it's very it can be kind of confusing what to do with that.
所以，面对这些时，确实会让人感到困惑，不知道该怎么处理。

1231
00:56:11.560 --> 00:56:15.180
And then, of course, I had spent 10 years not working at all.
当然，我曾经有十年时间完全没有工作。

1232
00:56:15.540 --> 00:56:19.080
So you're like, yeah, yeah, I don't want I mean, I don't want to go back to that, I guess.
所以你会想，是啊，我不想回到那种状态，我想大概是这样。

1233
00:56:19.220 --> 00:56:19.820
So I don't know.
所以我也不确定。

1234
00:56:20.180 --> 00:56:20.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1235
00:56:20.840 --> 00:56:25.360
I think for me, I would look back and just tell myself I'm going to be just fine.
我想如果是我，我会回顾过去，告诉自己：我会过得很好的。

1236
00:56:25.600 --> 00:56:38.900
I think I was just worried that I wasn't going to be everything I was thought I should be and that I don't need to be anything other than just OK with myself.
我想我当时只是担心自己无法成为别人眼中那个“应该成为”的人，但我其实不需要成为别的什么，只要能坦然面对自己就足够了。

1237
00:56:39.320 --> 00:56:40.180
That's what I think.
我是这么想的。

1238
00:56:40.180 --> 00:56:53.060
It's interesting how similar there's sort of like like success on somebody else's terms is not success and success on your own terms doesn't have to look like somebody else's or like the sort of consensus aspiration.
很有趣，那种基于他人标准定义的成功，其实并不是真正的成功；而基于你自己标准定义的成功，并不一定非要看起来像别人的成功，或者那种大众所追求的愿景。

1239
00:56:53.420 --> 00:56:53.500
Right.
没错。

1240
00:56:53.600 --> 00:56:57.180
It's like you and to be like, I'm basically I'm enough.
就像你，你要意识到，我本质上已经足够好了。

1241
00:56:57.400 --> 00:56:58.180
Who I am is enough.
我本身就足够了。

1242
00:56:58.320 --> 00:56:59.340
What I want is enough.
我想要的已经足够了。

1243
00:56:59.440 --> 00:56:59.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1244
00:57:00.020 --> 00:57:06.060
I think then that was something in that blog post that made an impression on me when I read it, too, which is I think I don't remember the exact phrasing.
我想那篇博文里有一点给我留下了深刻印象，虽然我不记得确切的措辞了。

1245
00:57:06.180 --> 00:57:07.740
It was basically like don't postpone joy.
大意就是不要推迟快乐。

1246
00:57:07.740 --> 00:57:13.220
Don't make a certain kind of professional success a prerequisite for participating in your own life.
不要把某种职业上的成功，当作参与自己生活的先决条件。

1247
00:57:13.380 --> 00:57:14.460
That's my recollection.
我是这么记得的。

1248
00:57:14.780 --> 00:57:14.980
Yeah.
是啊。

1249
00:57:15.080 --> 00:57:18.380
Well, that was a thing when you're a struggling actor, especially you're like, well,
嗯，当你是个苦苦挣扎的演员时，情况确实如此，你会想，嗯，

1250
00:57:18.420 --> 00:57:22.920
I can't go to my friend's wedding because I might get a callback for a thing that I auditioned for.
我不能去参加朋友的婚礼，因为我可能会接到试镜的回电。

1251
00:57:22.920 --> 00:57:26.180
So I need to be here or whatever it is.
所以我得待在这儿，或者诸如此类的。

1252
00:57:26.180 --> 00:57:29.460
It's like, well, I don't want to have a boyfriend because I don't want to be distracted.
就像是，嗯，我不想交男朋友，因为我不想分心。

1253
00:57:29.460 --> 00:57:39.540
There's like all these limits and all these superstitions that you have as an artist because you are holding the art as the only thing, the only aspiration.
作为艺术家，你会给自己设下各种限制和迷信，因为你把艺术视为唯一的事物，唯一的追求。

1254
00:57:39.900 --> 00:57:52.680
And so what I found was, oh, my gosh, the material and characters that I saw at that wedding and that life experience I got from going to that thing is just going to feed my art.
所以我发现，天哪，我在那场婚礼上看到的素材和人物，以及我从那次经历中获得的生活体验，都将成为我艺术创作的养分。

1255
00:57:52.680 --> 00:57:56.820
So it's like you can't do art if you're just doing art.
所以说，如果你只是为了做艺术而做艺术，那是行不通的。

1256
00:57:56.980 --> 00:57:57.140
Right.
没错。

1257
00:57:57.200 --> 00:57:59.980
I think you have to have a whole life in order to feed it.
我认为你必须拥有完整的生活，才能为艺术提供滋养。

1258
00:58:00.400 --> 00:58:06.180
And an identity that's like where you're like self-esteem is a little bit more like diversified.
还要有一种身份认同，让你的自尊心变得更加多元化。

1259
00:58:06.180 --> 00:58:12.740
In other words, if your whole worth originates from your ability to do this one thing and you're not doing that one thing, then you're kind of a ghoSt.
换句话说，如果你的全部价值都源于你做这一件事的能力，而当你没在做这件事时，你就仿佛成了一个幽灵。

1260
00:58:13.580 --> 00:58:16.540
So like to have like if you're like, oh, yeah, I'm not just an actor.
所以，如果你能说，哦，是的，我不只是个演员。

1261
00:58:16.720 --> 00:58:20.120
I'm someone's mom or I'm someone's right, you know, or I'm or not someone's.
我是某人的妈妈，或者我是某人的，你知道，或者我不是谁的谁。

1262
00:58:20.180 --> 00:58:21.220
I am a mom.
我是一位母亲。

1263
00:58:21.360 --> 00:58:23.740
I am a bicycle enthusiaSt.
我是一位自行车爱好者。

1264
00:58:23.840 --> 00:58:25.040
I am a whatever a volunteer.
我是一位志愿者，或者别的什么。

1265
00:58:25.300 --> 00:58:30.520
I you know, then you then it's not like, oh, when I'm auditioning for a part, I'm auditioning for my self-worth.
你知道，这样的话，当你去试镜某个角色时，就不会觉得是在拿自己的自我价值去冒险。

1266
00:58:30.800 --> 00:58:32.400
It's like I'm just auditioning for the part.
就像我只是在为这个角色试镜而已。

1267
00:58:32.660 --> 00:58:35.840
It's like, yeah, which is hard enough or daunting enough.
没错，这已经够难、够让人望而生畏的了。

1268
00:58:35.980 --> 00:58:36.580
That makes sense.
很有道理。

1269
00:58:36.680 --> 00:58:37.140
That's beautiful.
说得真好。

1270
00:58:37.480 --> 00:58:38.360
What about you, Zach?
你呢，扎克？

1271
00:58:38.600 --> 00:58:40.240
What would you go back and tell yourself?
你会回去告诉自己什么？

1272
00:58:40.740 --> 00:58:42.040
Get a basket at Walmart.
在沃尔玛拿个购物篮吧。

1273
00:58:42.040 --> 00:58:46.060
If you're going to be carrying that many humidifiers, I was basically like a walk in close call video.
如果你要搬那么多加湿器，我当时简直就像个行走的灾难现场。

1274
00:58:46.880 --> 00:58:51.340
I think I tell myself it's something similar.
我想我会告诉自己类似的话。

1275
00:58:51.460 --> 00:58:52.340
It's like it's an interesting.
这很有意思。

1276
00:58:53.420 --> 00:58:54.160
I don't know.
我不知道。

1277
00:58:54.220 --> 00:58:55.140
Let me think for a second.
让我思考一下。

1278
00:58:57.260 --> 00:58:58.140
I think.
我想。

1279
00:58:59.520 --> 00:59:06.800
I think I probably would try to tell myself and I probably wouldn't be able to hear it, but like you don't need so much fear to protect you.
我想我可能会试着告诉自己——虽然我可能听不进去——你不需要那么多恐惧来保护自己。

1280
00:59:07.040 --> 00:59:07.420
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1281
00:59:07.460 --> 00:59:12.900
Like I think I used anxiety as a kind of as a motivator and as a kind of protection.
我觉得我曾把焦虑当作一种动力，一种保护机制。

1282
00:59:12.900 --> 00:59:18.980
Where I sort of felt like, well, if I'm buying enough humidifiers and running my lines enough times and freaking out enough,
我当时觉得，嗯，如果我买了足够多的加湿器，把台词背了足够多遍，并且足够抓狂，

1283
00:59:19.080 --> 00:59:21.880
then surely I'm doing everything in my power to do a good job.
那么我肯定已经尽我所能把工作做好了。

1284
00:59:22.000 --> 00:59:25.980
And if I don't do that, then I'm going to be kind of culpable if it doesn't go well.
如果我不这样做，那如果事情进展不顺，我就会有不可推卸的责任。

1285
00:59:26.420 --> 00:59:34.680
I think if I could go back and say like when you're doing all of that, it has more to do with like it's more neurotic than artistic.
我想如果我能回去告诉自己，当你做那些事的时候，那更多是神经质，而不是艺术创作。

1286
00:59:35.200 --> 00:59:35.620
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1287
00:59:35.740 --> 00:59:37.500
It's not that actually isn't serving.
那其实并没有什么帮助。

1288
00:59:38.060 --> 00:59:38.880
It's not really.
真的没有。

1289
00:59:39.020 --> 00:59:43.420
Hopefully it doesn't hurt the character or the work, but it's about something different.
希望这不会伤害到角色或作品，但这完全是另一回事。

1290
00:59:43.480 --> 00:59:47.080
That's more about like your childhood than it is about the job you're doing.
那更多是关于你的童年，而不是你正在做的工作。

1291
00:59:47.620 --> 00:59:52.780
And so I think if I could be like, don't mistake your neuroses for your artistic process,
所以我想，如果我能对自己说，别把你的神经质误认为是你的艺术创作过程，

1292
00:59:53.040 --> 01:00:03.860
like develop an artistic process independent of that as much as possible so that you're not just reenacting your own like cuckoo bird story again and again at work.
尽可能独立于此去发展一套艺术创作流程，这样你就不会在工作中一遍又一遍地重演你那套疯狂的故事了。

1293
01:00:04.100 --> 01:00:05.340
Like tell a new story at work.
在工作中讲个新故事吧。

1294
01:00:05.460 --> 01:00:06.740
Tell someone else's story at work.
在工作中讲讲别人的故事。

1295
01:00:06.860 --> 01:00:07.400
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1296
01:00:07.400 --> 01:00:17.060
I think you I think you did hear it because I think just the fact that you recognize it, that even though I mean, it took a minute, took many minutes.
我觉得你其实听进去了，因为仅仅是你意识到这一点，尽管——我是说，这花了一点时间，花了很多时间。

1297
01:00:17.500 --> 01:00:18.660
What was your second question?
你的第二个问题是什么？

1298
01:00:19.380 --> 01:00:20.200
Oh, yes.
哦，对了。

1299
01:00:20.400 --> 01:00:25.800
Second question is like, did you have a moment where you felt that kind of like because so often I think when you get the thing that you want,
第二个问题是，你有没有过那种感觉，因为我常觉得当你得到了你想要的东西时，

1300
01:00:25.920 --> 01:00:27.980
it doesn't feel the way you thought it'd feel, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah.
它感觉并不像你想象的那样，诸如此类，等等等等。

1301
01:00:28.080 --> 01:00:31.020
Like the behind the music kind of like thing.
就像那种幕后花絮一样。

1302
01:00:31.020 --> 01:00:40.320
Was there a moment, though, where you had that kind of like shimmering magic feeling like where you're like looked around and you were like, oh, my God,
不过，有没有那么一个瞬间，你感受到了一种闪闪发光的魔力，就像你环顾四周，心想，天哪，

1303
01:00:40.640 --> 01:00:48.260
like that moment where you're just like the sort of the gift of it where you felt like really wholly present in it and able to just enjoy it.
就像那种你觉得这简直是上天馈赠的时刻，你完全沉浸其中，能够尽情享受它。

1304
01:00:48.360 --> 01:00:52.660
Like, do you remember that either the first or the most intense version of that for you guys?
你们还记得对你们来说，第一次或者最强烈的那种感觉是什么时候吗？

1305
01:00:52.660 --> 01:01:08.080
The first one for me was when we were shooting the pilot on the first day and our director, Ken Kwapis, said, I want to do 30 minutes of all of you all just working in this space.
对我来说，第一次是在我们拍摄试播集的第一天，我们的导演肯·夸皮斯说，我想让你们所有人都在这个空间里工作30分钟。

1306
01:01:08.280 --> 01:01:15.640
Do your job and we're just going to come around and silently document you like a documenter.
做好你们的工作，我们会像纪录片拍摄者一样，悄悄地在周围记录你们。

1307
01:01:15.720 --> 01:01:17.720
We're going to set the tone of this show.
我们要为这部剧定下基调。

1308
01:01:18.280 --> 01:01:19.520
All right, go ahead.
好了，开始吧。

1309
01:01:19.520 --> 01:01:40.440
All right, go ahead.
好了，开始吧。

1310
01:01:51.780 --> 01:01:56.980
And I was like, the theater nerd in me was delighted.
当时我就觉得，我内心那个戏剧书呆子简直乐坏了。

1311
01:01:57.580 --> 01:02:01.800
And I thought I'm a part of something very special.
我心想，我正在参与一件非常特别的事情。

1312
01:02:01.800 --> 01:02:06.780
And I don't know what's going to happen from here, but this is pretty dang cool.
我不知道接下来会发生什么，但这真的太酷了。

1313
01:02:08.260 --> 01:02:08.780
Wow.
哇。

1314
01:02:09.500 --> 01:02:12.660
The sound, it just sounds like an orchestra tuning up.
那声音，听起来就像管弦乐队在调音一样。

1315
01:02:12.780 --> 01:02:13.100
Yes, yeah.
没错，是的。

1316
01:02:13.100 --> 01:02:15.260
Like, here we go, we're about to play.
就像是，我们要开始了，我们要准备表演了。

1317
01:02:15.420 --> 01:02:17.560
Like, wow, that's so exciting.
哇，那真是太令人兴奋了。

1318
01:02:17.940 --> 01:02:19.120
I really felt that.
我真的感受到了。

1319
01:02:19.120 --> 01:02:19.660
Yeah.
是啊。

1320
01:02:20.080 --> 01:02:23.100
I mean, yeah, I loved that so much.
我是说，是的，我太喜欢那种感觉了。

1321
01:02:23.640 --> 01:02:27.260
For me, there's so many moments that felt like that.
对我来说，有太多时刻都有那种感觉了。

1322
01:02:27.260 --> 01:02:35.440
And they were almost always in the conference room because we were all in there together and we were all each other's background.
而且它们几乎总是发生在会议室里，因为我们都在那里，互为彼此的背景。

1323
01:02:38.660 --> 01:02:45.440
And so many times I would have a minute where I was in the scene, but then I would step out of my body.
很多时候，我会在戏里待上一分钟，然后我就感觉灵魂出窍了。

1324
01:02:45.440 --> 01:02:52.900
And I would just watch these amazing actors just fire off all these lines and everyone had their own character backstory.
我只是看着这些出色的演员们抛出一个个台词，每个人都有自己的角色背景故事。

1325
01:02:53.580 --> 01:02:59.400
And I just would be there in awe, being like, this is so cool, this is so cool, and I get to do this.
我当时就在那里惊叹，心想，这太酷了，这太酷了，我竟然能参与其中。

1326
01:02:59.400 --> 01:03:00.880
And there were times my character.
有时候我的角色。

1327
01:03:00.880 --> 01:03:04.560
And there were times my character didn't even have lines, but I just couldn't believe I was in the moment.
有时候我的角色甚至没有台词，但我简直不敢相信我正身处那一刻。

1328
01:03:04.820 --> 01:03:09.820
There was a scene where Michael Scott is brainstorming animal hybrids.
有一场戏是迈克尔·斯科特在头脑风暴各种动物杂交品种。

1329
01:03:11.400 --> 01:03:13.780
And no one is saying anything.
当时没人说话。

1330
01:03:14.320 --> 01:03:21.220
And Steve had his scripted lines, but then he started to just, they just let the camera roll and he just kept improvising animal hybrids.
史蒂夫有剧本台词，但他开始，他们就让摄像机一直开着，他就不停地即兴创作各种动物杂交品种。

1331
01:03:21.300 --> 01:03:29.560
And we all just had to sit there and look at him where he was like, head of an owl, body of a walrus, like whatever it was he was saying.
我们所有人都得坐在那里看着他，他说什么猫头鹰的头、海象的身体之类的，不管他说什么。

1332
01:03:29.560 --> 01:03:32.760
And we were just all patiently looking at him.
我们都只是耐心地看着他。

1333
01:03:32.820 --> 01:03:36.660
And then one by one, people started to file out like they were over it.
然后大家开始一个接一个地走出去，好像他们已经受够了。

1334
01:03:36.820 --> 01:03:40.360
And I just remember being like, this is one of, this is the cooleSt.
我记得当时我就想，这是，这是最酷的。

1335
01:03:40.740 --> 01:03:43.640
Like, this is the coolest, and I can't believe I get to do it.
就像，这是最酷的，我简直不敢相信我能做这个。

1336
01:03:43.860 --> 01:03:48.960
It's so sweet that in both your cases, it's sort of like, it's not the kind of Grand Slam scene for your character.
你们两人的情况都很温馨，这并不是那种对你们角色来说的“全垒打”式重头戏。

1337
01:03:49.140 --> 01:03:56.480
It's just the scene where you're able to kind of like behold the majesty of this working situation, right?
这只是一个让你能够见证这种工作环境之宏大的场景，对吧？

1338
01:03:56.480 --> 01:04:00.760
Where you're like, it's about watching it and participating, but not in a way that foregrounds you.
就像是，重点在于观察和参与，但不是以那种让你成为焦点的方式。

1339
01:04:00.920 --> 01:04:06.560
It's just a, I think like being a small part of a big thing is like the best feeling ever, right?
我觉得成为一件大事的一小部分是世界上最棒的感觉，对吧？

1340
01:04:06.640 --> 01:04:11.180
Like, like feeling like you're part of a squad that like is like, that's such an exciting.
就像，感觉自己是团队的一部分，那种感觉真的太令人兴奋了。

1341
01:04:11.340 --> 01:04:14.920
So it's interesting, both of you guys, it was kind of like that feeling of like, oh, I'm part of this.
所以很有趣，你们俩都有那种感觉，就是“哦，我是其中的一部分”。

1342
01:04:15.120 --> 01:04:20.860
When everyone starts improvising the filing out and Michael's still doing his animals, right?
当大家开始即兴地走出去，而迈克尔还在继续他的动物表演时，对吧？

1343
01:04:21.000 --> 01:04:26.400
Or everyone sort of slowly coming into the joining, showing up for the first time.
或者大家慢慢加入进来，第一次出现在镜头里。

1344
01:04:26.480 --> 01:04:28.120
I'm in the fictional office in a way.
某种程度上，我就在那个虚构的办公室里。

1345
01:04:28.300 --> 01:04:33.560
It was such a smart thing that Ken did by doing that exercise with us because we didn't start with a scene.
肯做的那个练习真是太聪明了，因为我们不是从一场戏开始的。

1346
01:04:33.720 --> 01:04:39.860
Like, we didn't start with, okay, Steve Carell, our lead character, Michael Scott is going to do a scene.
我们不是从“好，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔，我们的主角迈克尔·斯科特要演一场戏”开始的。

1347
01:04:40.200 --> 01:04:45.500
He made every single one of us equally important in the very first thing we shot.
他在我们拍摄的第一件事中，让每一个人的重要性都同等重要。

1348
01:04:45.740 --> 01:04:46.220
Wow.
哇。

1349
01:04:46.220 --> 01:04:57.860
You know, nobody had any lines, but everyone was in character and you really felt how, okay, so whatever scene is going on, this is also always going on.
你知道，没人有台词，但每个人都在角色里，你真的能感觉到，无论正在发生什么戏，这（办公室工作）也总是在进行中。

1350
01:04:58.020 --> 01:05:04.820
So now we're going to do a scene, but don't forget, you all are still working in this office and you always have to be.
所以现在我们要演一场戏了，但别忘了，你们所有人仍然在这个办公室里工作，而且你们必须一直保持这种状态。

1351
01:05:04.960 --> 01:05:05.880
It was really genius.
那真是太天才了。

1352
01:05:06.280 --> 01:05:06.960
That's cool.
那很酷。

1353
01:05:07.220 --> 01:05:08.500
I didn't, I think I missed that.
我没注意到，我想我错过了。

1354
01:05:08.640 --> 01:05:11.140
It was the first, literally the first thing you shot.
那是第一场，真的是你拍的第一场戏。

1355
01:05:11.260 --> 01:05:12.460
The very first thing.
绝对是第一场。

1356
01:05:12.460 --> 01:05:12.840
Brilliant.
太棒了。

1357
01:05:13.060 --> 01:05:13.240
Ever.
有史以来最好的。

1358
01:05:13.900 --> 01:05:15.600
First time the cameras rolled, right?
摄像机第一次转动的时候，对吧？

1359
01:05:15.820 --> 01:05:16.020
Yeah.
没错。

1360
01:05:16.240 --> 01:05:16.640
I know.
我知道。

1361
01:05:16.980 --> 01:05:23.660
Just give everyone a chance to kind of, it's sort of what John did for me when I did that little talking head where it was like, okay, just like, I mean,
就是给每个人一个机会，有点像约翰当初为我做的那样，当时我拍那个小访谈片段，就像是，好吧，就是，我是说，

1362
01:05:23.700 --> 01:05:26.900
that's different because I was like talking, but I just mean like giving a lot of space.
那不一样，因为当时我在说话，但我只是指那种留出很大空间的感觉。

1363
01:05:27.040 --> 01:05:27.260
Yes.
是的。

1364
01:05:27.480 --> 01:05:28.640
Even though it was, even that's costly.
尽管那样做，即使那样也是很昂贵的。

1365
01:05:28.740 --> 01:05:31.120
You're making a pilot, like time is money, everything, right?
你在拍试播集，时间就是金钱，一切都是，对吧？

1366
01:05:31.120 --> 01:05:35.080
Like, but just to be like, we got time, we got space, just exiSt.
就像是，但只是说，我们有时间，我们有空间，只要存在就好。

1367
01:05:35.500 --> 01:05:43.160
And I also think because it was Ken, the very first time we were all in a room and we were all going to be these characters, no one yelled action.
而且我也觉得因为那是肯，我们第一次聚在一个房间里，准备扮演这些角色时，没有人喊“开始”。

1368
01:05:43.780 --> 01:05:45.620
He just said, go ahead.
他只是说，开始吧。

1369
01:05:46.180 --> 01:05:46.980
Oh, that's nice.
哦，那真好。

1370
01:05:47.260 --> 01:05:47.700
Because that's Ken, right?
因为那就是肯，对吧？

1371
01:05:47.800 --> 01:05:48.640
So he just said, go ahead.
所以他只是说，开始吧。

1372
01:05:48.960 --> 01:05:54.100
So it was just like this very slow, comfortable easing into this world.
所以那就像是一种非常缓慢、舒适地进入这个世界的过程。

1373
01:05:54.520 --> 01:05:56.660
Did you ever see that John Cazale documentary?
你看过那部关于约翰·卡扎尔的纪录片吗？

1374
01:05:56.900 --> 01:05:59.180
I knew it was, do you know John Cazale, the guy who played Fredo?
我知道那是，你认识约翰·卡扎尔吗，就是演弗雷多那个人？

1375
01:05:59.180 --> 01:06:05.600
So he was like in five movies and they're all like, but he was like in Deer Hunter, Godfather 1 and 2, The Conversation.
他一共就演了五部电影，每一部都，但他演了《猎鹿人》、《教父1和2》、《对话》。

1376
01:06:06.300 --> 01:06:11.900
He died when he was a young man, but they made a documentary about him because he did these like incredible movies and that's it.
他英年早逝，但人们为他拍了一部纪录片，因为他演了这些不可思议的电影，仅此而已。

1377
01:06:12.060 --> 01:06:13.560
He just did these and then theater and stuff.
他只演了这些，然后就是戏剧之类的。

1378
01:06:13.800 --> 01:06:16.140
But Al Pacino, oh, he was in Dog Day Afternoon.
但是阿尔·帕西诺，哦，他演了《热天午后》。

1379
01:06:16.580 --> 01:06:24.920
Al Pacino told these stories where they'd be like shooting on film and they would start rolling and Al Pacino would be all kind of coiled up and do his line.
阿尔·帕西诺讲过这些故事，说他们当时在用胶片拍摄，摄像机开始转动，阿尔·帕西诺会整个人紧绷起来，准备说台词。

1380
01:06:25.140 --> 01:06:28.740
And he said, this guy, the John Cazale would just be like, what'd you do this weekend, Al?
他说，这家伙，约翰·卡扎尔，就会问：你周末做了什么，阿尔？

1381
01:06:29.180 --> 01:06:36.980
And he'd hear the film moving through the camera and he'd be like, uh, I don't know, I like made dinner with my girlfriend on Saturday.
他能听到胶片在摄像机里转动的声音，然后他会说：呃，我不知道，我周六和女朋友做了顿晚餐。

1382
01:06:37.080 --> 01:06:37.780
Oh, yeah, what'd you make?
哦，是吗，你做了什么？

1383
01:06:38.520 --> 01:06:43.120
Oh, we made a rigatoni and, you know, oh, yeah, what'd you do after that?
哦，我们做了通心粉，你知道，哦，是吗，那之后你做了什么？

1384
01:06:43.260 --> 01:06:46.640
And like just talk until like Al Pacino settled down.
就这样一直聊，直到阿尔·帕西诺平静下来。

1385
01:06:46.640 --> 01:06:53.240
And then he'd just say like the first line of the scene where like he would just sort of get them in a place of like, oh, we're just here.
然后他才会说出那场戏的第一句台词，他就是那种会把他们带入一种状态的人，就像是，哦，我们就在这儿。

1386
01:06:53.460 --> 01:06:54.400
We're just here with each other.
我们只是彼此陪伴在这里。

1387
01:06:54.600 --> 01:06:57.540
And then slowly sort of introduce the dialogue.
然后慢慢地引入对话。

1388
01:06:57.540 --> 01:07:00.380
It's just like such a ballsy, crazy thing to do.
这真是一件大胆又疯狂的事情。

1389
01:07:00.400 --> 01:07:00.560
Yes.
是的。

1390
01:07:00.660 --> 01:07:02.820
Where like 35 millimeter film is running through a camera.
当时35毫米胶片正在摄像机里转动着。

1391
01:07:03.000 --> 01:07:06.280
But I just was like, it sounds like in a version of that, right?
但我当时就觉得，这听起来像是那种方式的变体，对吧？

1392
01:07:06.380 --> 01:07:07.120
Where it's just like, go ahead.
就像是，开始吧。

1393
01:07:07.260 --> 01:07:07.620
Yeah, go ahead.
对，开始吧。

1394
01:07:07.880 --> 01:07:09.580
We're not, it's not ready, set, go.
我们不是，不是那种“预备，开始”。

1395
01:07:09.580 --> 01:07:11.100
Hit your adding machine a few times.
按几下你的计算器。

1396
01:07:11.100 --> 01:07:12.440
Yeah, that's nice.
是啊，那真好。

1397
01:07:12.620 --> 01:07:12.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1398
01:07:13.040 --> 01:07:13.800
I feel bad.
我感到很抱歉。

1399
01:07:13.920 --> 01:07:15.960
I feel like I've now distended your.
我觉得我现在打乱了你的。

1400
01:07:15.980 --> 01:07:16.240
No, are you kidding?
不，你在开玩笑吗？

1401
01:07:16.280 --> 01:07:16.540
Okay.
好的。

1402
01:07:16.700 --> 01:07:18.180
I love this so much.
我太喜欢这个了。

1403
01:07:18.180 --> 01:07:19.740
It's just made my heart so happy.
它让我的内心感到无比快乐。

1404
01:07:19.820 --> 01:07:20.280
Me too.
我也是。

1405
01:07:20.640 --> 01:07:20.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1406
01:07:21.060 --> 01:07:23.060
And I really, yeah, I can't say it enough.
而且我真的，没错，我怎么说都不够。

1407
01:07:23.220 --> 01:07:33.040
Like it's, it's a real talent I don't have, which is like to maintain like, you know, did you ever see those like Richard Linklater, the like before sunset, before sunrise.
就像，这是一种我所不具备的真正天赋，就是那种，你知道，你看过理查德·林克莱特拍的那些电影吗，比如《爱在日落黄昏时》、《爱在黎明破晓前》之类的。

1408
01:07:33.360 --> 01:07:33.760
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

1409
01:07:33.800 --> 01:07:34.500
I love those movies.
我超爱那些电影。

1410
01:07:34.720 --> 01:07:41.020
But that's sometimes what like shooting feels like to me, where it's like this like very discreet, specific experience of like real, like.
但有时拍戏给我的感觉就是那样，就像是一种非常谨慎、具体的体验，非常真实。

1411
01:07:41.100 --> 01:07:43.180
Big emotion, intimacy, connection.
强烈的情感、亲密感、联结感。

1412
01:07:43.480 --> 01:07:49.820
And then you're like off to your lives and you don't, to me, it often feels that way where it's like, it's like this amazing one night stand or something,
然后你们就各自回归生活了，对我来说，那种感觉就像是一场美妙的露水情缘之类的，

1413
01:07:49.920 --> 01:07:52.380
except it happened to be a two year stand.
只不过这次持续了两年。

1414
01:07:52.540 --> 01:08:01.120
But, and so I feel like I've kind of lost touch with, you know, you guys and this larger squad.
但是，我觉得自己好像和你们，还有这个大团队失去联系了。

1415
01:08:01.120 --> 01:08:06.860
But I can just never say enough how much it meant that everyone was so kind.
但我永远无法表达出大家当时对我那么好意味着什么。

1416
01:08:07.280 --> 01:08:11.000
I just, in a way that you guys stood to gain nothing from that.
你们当时完全没必要那样做，也没能从中得到什么好处。

1417
01:08:11.180 --> 01:08:12.440
I had nothing to offer you.
我当时也没什么能给你们的。

1418
01:08:12.580 --> 01:08:21.600
And in a way I could have been either in your, like I could have been a problem in that it's like another mouth to feed on this big show.
从某种程度上说，我甚至可能成为你们的麻烦，就像在这个大剧组里多了一张要吃饭的嘴。

1419
01:08:21.600 --> 01:08:24.460
Like, but that was not how I was received.
但是，我并没有受到那样的对待。

1420
01:08:24.460 --> 01:08:29.300
And that really set the tone for the rest of my working life thus far.
这真的为我迄今为止的职业生涯定下了基调。

1421
01:08:29.460 --> 01:08:32.780
And it's, so I just, yeah, I don't know.
所以，我只是，嗯，我不知道。

1422
01:08:32.980 --> 01:08:33.860
I just want it.
我只是想说。

1423
01:08:33.940 --> 01:08:45.560
I felt, when you guys kindly invited me on, I was like, I want to say to people, I want people who like the show to know how kind the people who worked on the show were and are,
当你们好心邀请我参加时，我就想，我想告诉大家，我想让喜欢这部剧的人知道，参与制作这部剧的人过去和现在都非常善良，

1424
01:08:45.700 --> 01:08:46.100
you know.
你知道的。

1425
01:08:46.100 --> 01:08:57.200
You know, I think we were happy, Zach, like we were a happy cast, we were a happy crew, and we just knew, like, there's enough to go around for everyone.
你知道，我觉得我们很幸福，扎克，我们是一个快乐的演员阵容，一个快乐的剧组，我们都知道，机会足够每个人分享。

1426
01:08:57.740 --> 01:08:58.740
There just is.
确实如此。

1427
01:08:58.880 --> 01:08:59.800
There always is.
一直都是这样。

1428
01:08:59.800 --> 01:09:04.240
In good comedy and good art, you do not need to be stingy, you know.
在好的喜剧和好的艺术中，你不需要吝啬，你知道的。

1429
01:09:04.260 --> 01:09:04.920
It's a collective.
这是一个集体。

1430
01:09:05.280 --> 01:09:05.640
It is.
确实是。

1431
01:09:05.640 --> 01:09:09.040
And it was an abundant universe, and I think we all looked at it that way.
那是一个资源丰富的世界，我想我们都是这样看待它的。

1432
01:09:09.140 --> 01:09:11.040
We always felt like we won the lottery.
我们总觉得像是中了彩票一样。

1433
01:09:11.080 --> 01:09:12.580
We always talk about that.
我们总是谈论这个。

1434
01:09:12.940 --> 01:09:14.520
And I think everyone felt that way.
我想每个人都有同感。

1435
01:09:14.520 --> 01:09:16.260
So, why not share it?
所以，为什么不分享呢？

1436
01:09:16.800 --> 01:09:21.760
A lot of lottery winners hire, like, private security and, like, a bunch of Dobermans and shit.
很多中彩票的人会雇私人保镖，养一堆杜宾犬之类的。

1437
01:09:22.040 --> 01:09:26.080
You guys are, like, you know, you guys are, like, the good lottery winners.
你们就像是，你知道，你们是那种善良的彩票中奖者。

1438
01:09:27.240 --> 01:09:29.100
Zach, thank you so much for coming on.
扎克，非常感谢你来参加节目。

1439
01:09:29.100 --> 01:09:30.080
Thank you for having me.
谢谢你们邀请我。

1440
01:09:30.180 --> 01:09:30.760
It was really fun.
真的很有趣。

1441
01:09:30.860 --> 01:09:33.320
What are you doing now that we can tell people about?
你现在在做什么我们可以告诉大家的事情吗？

1442
01:09:33.440 --> 01:09:40.460
I'm making this stop motion show that, actually, Greg Daniels is, like, he's, it's his company, but it is one of the producers on.
我正在制作一部定格动画剧，其实是格雷格·丹尼尔斯的公司，他是制片人之一。

1443
01:09:40.460 --> 01:09:46.180
It's a stop motion show about an NPR host, so I'm doing that right now, and that'll come out.
那是一部关于 NPR 主持人的定格动画，我正在做这个，到时候会播出。

1444
01:09:46.280 --> 01:09:47.880
Are you the voice of the NPR host?
你是那个 NPR 主持人的配音吗？

1445
01:09:48.200 --> 01:09:48.260
Yeah.
是的。

1446
01:09:49.060 --> 01:09:49.420
Amazing.
太棒了。

1447
01:09:49.540 --> 01:09:53.080
You'll have to let us know when it comes out and where people can find it, and we're going to share it.
到时候一定要告诉我们什么时候播出，在哪里可以看到，我们会帮你宣传的。

1448
01:09:53.240 --> 01:09:54.060
Oh, that's so sweet.
噢，那太贴心了。

1449
01:09:54.220 --> 01:09:54.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1450
01:09:54.420 --> 01:09:56.000
But anyway, thanks for having me on.
总之，谢谢你们邀请我。

1451
01:09:56.080 --> 01:09:56.580
It was really a treat.
这真是一次难得的享受。

1452
01:09:56.740 --> 01:09:58.140
It's so nice to reconnect with you guys.
能和你们重新取得联系真是太好了。

1453
01:09:58.200 --> 01:09:58.760
Nice to see you.
很高兴见到你们。

1454
01:09:58.800 --> 01:09:59.500
Love you, Zach.
爱你，扎克。

1455
01:09:59.660 --> 01:10:00.240
Yeah, you too.
是啊，我也是。

1456
01:10:06.510 --> 01:10:08.330
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1457
01:10:08.610 --> 01:10:12.730
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由Earwolf、珍娜·费舍和安吉拉·金赛制作。

1458
01:10:12.930 --> 01:10:15.110
Our senior producer is Cassie Jerkins.
我们的高级制作人是凯西·杰金斯。

1459
01:10:15.310 --> 01:10:17.390
Our in-studio engineer is Sam Kiefer.
我们的演播室工程师是萨姆·基弗。

1460
01:10:17.530 --> 01:10:22.130
Our editing and mixing engineer is Jordan Duffy, and our associate producer is Ainsley Bubaco.
我们的剪辑和混音工程师是乔丹·达菲，我们的助理制作人是安斯利·布巴科。

1461
01:10:22.410 --> 01:10:25.270
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是克里德·布拉顿创作的《橡胶树》。
